    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n93951" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σῐβύνη</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῠ], ἡ</span>, and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σῐβύνης</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῠ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>, ὁ</span>,
			<i><span class="en">
			Alex.
			131
		</span></i> (fem.), <i><span class="en">
			<u>AP</u>
			7.421
		</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
			Mel.
		</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
			6.93
		</span></i> (Antip., masc.):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>hunting spear</i>, and generally, <i>spear, pike</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				18.27
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				20.33
			</span></i>:—also written <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζιβύνη</span></b>  (q.v.), <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συβίνη</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
				<u>PCair.Zen.</u>
				362.34
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>, cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συ[μ]βίνη[ς</span>] (post <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συβήνη</span>)<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">: καπροβόλον,
				ἐμβόλιον</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>, but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σιγύνης [ῡ</span>] is prob.
			not related. (Illyrian acc. to Fest.<i><span class="en">
				p.453
			</span></i> L., citing Ennius.)</div>
